NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1043,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,3,4,2,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.4606,"rank":0.0,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"YPFOE127c","role":"top","render":{"description":"When the skippers go ashore, they hear at night hammering on the wooden ships. It sounds as if a number of men are at work, but when the skippers go to look, there is nothing to be seen.","place":"Nieuwe Bildtzijl","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"SINSAG 0061","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12976","half":"top"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"YPFOE127c","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"When the skippers are in bed, the sound starts again. It also happens that when workmen arrive in the peat bog, at night they hear full wheelbarrows going over the planks, and then hear a load of sand being dumped.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0061"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ096502","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"We then heard the \"foresound\" of the threshing.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0061"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"Voda_022_18","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Two days later a funeral procession passed that spot.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0481"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ037801","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A year later a fire did break out at that spot.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0491"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ060703","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"So she says that Drachten will become a big town with factories and wealth. It came true.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ071705","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Once she saw a coffin with a white cloth over it. Then she knew that a woman would soon die in childbed. That came true.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0483"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"CJ064204","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Nobody wants to sleep in it because a dead man once lay in it. At night you are shaken back and forth in it, and the machines do not stop during the night. That night, however, the old man is not shaken back and forth, but the machines are constantly moving and do not stay in the same place.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0061"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"CJ012712","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Years later he courted a woman with jet-black hair, and to reach her he had to cross the same water twice by a little bridge.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"GENDT168","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Both come true.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"CJ118607","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It is an omen: later a dike is built on that spot.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"KEMP100","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It was Death, who always knocks on gate and door to take the last of a line along on the great journey.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0487"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ0007A02","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When she tells of it the horse is healthy, but a day later what she saw comes true.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0486"},"home":"1-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘skipper’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0061. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c2"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c2"],"stack":["c1","c2"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2279,"rank":0.4361,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1607","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Werewolves wore chains, so you could hear them coming from far away. People were upset then.","place":"Nieuwaal","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/125803","original":"Vroeger bij Sprokkelenburg onder Heukelum, daar woonde de machinist van 't stoomgemaal, die spookte daar ook. Van die verhalen dat d'r werwolve ware, diere met een ketting aan, dat je ze al van verre kon hore. De mense ware dan zo van streek.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ027402","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman once heard a lot of noise in an adjoining room. But there was nothing to see. The next day a relative fell through the floor and landed in that room. That was the sound the woman had heard the day before.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21587","original":"Ik wie op in kear by myn suster yn Twizelerheide. Wy sieten yn 't keammerke togearre by elkoar, doe hearde ik dat it der yn 'e oare keamer hiel bot oan wei gong. Myn suster fornaem it net. Ik sei: \"Hwat in lawaei.\" Wy der hinne. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Dat wy gongen wer nei 't keammerke ta to thédrinken.\nDe oare deis rekke de dochter fan myn suster troch de souder hinne boppe de keamer. De planken bijoegen har. Dat joech in stik leven. En dàt hie ik de foarige deis heard.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ026709","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman often hears a voice in her dreams that makes predictions to her. She also often hears the sound of hammering in places where new houses will be built.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21442","original":"Yn 'e droom hear ik faek in stem. Dy dielt my dan it ien of oare mei. Dêrtroch wyt ik fan alles, hwat der gebeure sil.\nIk haw trije beppesizzers, dy moesten alle trije in pop ha. Dy stem sei tsjin my: Twa derfan dat wurde jonges. Se komme allebeide Anders to hiten. (Ik wist net dat de heiten fan 'e manlju beide Anders hieten)\nTsjin 'e trêdde beppesizzer sei 'k: \"Dû krigest in famke.\" Dat is ek útkaem. It woarde tsjin my sein. Dat binne fisioenen.\nSa't ik sei, ik hear hiel faek timmerjen, sawol by dei as by nacht. En 't komt altyd nei.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ026702","role":"member","render":{"description":"One winter afternoon a woman heard a car in the yard, but she saw nothing. There were no car tracks to be found in the snow either. But the next day there was an accident on the road, and lots of people and cars came into the yard.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21435","original":"It gebeurde in pear jier lyn. 't Wie yn 'e winter, der lei snie. 't Wie op 'e neimiddei. Ik hearde in protte lawaei op 'e wei en by ús op it hiem. Ik hearde ek in greate auto. Doe't ik op it hiem kom wie der alhiel neat to sjen. En doe't ik de oare moarns doe't it ljocht wie, nei spoaren socht yn 'e snie, wienen dy der net. Doe wist ik it oare wol. De oare deis is hjir doe in ûngelok gebeurd op 'e wei. 't Wienen allegear auto's en minsken, ek hjir op it hiem. Se ha hjir doe noch in frou yn 'e hûs brocht.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Nieuwaal belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1281,"rank":0.3431,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"Voda_022_16","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A clergyman saw his own funeral. Four men with a bier kept walking behind him all night. He later died on that same road.","place":"Eindhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/129749","original":"Een geestelijke uit Oirschot zag eens zijn eigen begrafenis. Op een nacht ging hij van Oirschot naar Best. Daar hoorde hij achter zich iemand lopen. Toen ie omkeek, zag ie vier mannen die een baar droegen. Hij wilde wachten, maar toen hie stil bleef staan, bleven ook de dragers stilstaan. En als ie verder ging, gingen ook de dragers verder. Zo bleven deze vier mannen met de baar de gehele nacht achter de geestelijke lopen. Die was blij dat ie eindelijk in Best aankwam, waar hij van de schrik kon bekomen. Enige tijd later moest de geestelijke weer naar Best. Daar stierf hij plotseling. Toen droeg men het lijk van de geestelijke over dezelfde weg die hij gelopen had toen de dragers met de baar hem volgden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ099406","role":"omen","render":{"description":"When a dog howls eerily, someone in the neighbourhood will die within 4 days.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36651","original":"As in houn spûkgûlde seinen se, gong der binnen fjouwer dagen ien dea yn net to fiere omtrek.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ065203","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A group of boys once called names at an old woman who was said to be a witch. The woman made as if to jump across the four-metre ditch, and the boys ran off as fast as they could. She often had to get up at night to see funeral processions.","place":"Twijzelerheide","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27375","original":"Hjir wenne yn Twizelerheide in âld minske, dat wie Minne Ael, dy gong foar in tsjoenster troch. Hja wie nachts faek warber. Hja wenne oan 'e Swâdde. Dy wie sa'n fjouwer meter breed.\nOp in kear skelden in pear jonges har út, dy wienen oan 'e oare kant fan 'e Swâdde. Doe die se in pear stappen achterút en sei: \"Ik sil jim krije\", krekt as soe se in oanloop nimme.\nDoe naeiden dy jonges hurd út.\nHja moest der nachts út as der in lykstaesje ûnderweis wie.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","4 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":4},"on_success":{"chime":4,"digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P6","difficulty":3.2423,"rank":0.5736,"note":"Each story one number. In this order.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ006221","role":"clip1","render":{"description":"A woman is catching moles on the land with the eerie tree of the Bomklooster. Suddenly, some distance from her, two witte juffers (white maidens) walk across the land. When she goes over to look, they have vanished like snow before the sun.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16834","original":"In dochter fan Bouke Schievink wie us by 't maitiid oan 't mollebultstruijen op it lân fan Jan Binderts Kloosterman, fan 't Bomkleaster. Dat wie op dat stik lân mei de grouwe beam. Doe stapten dêr twa wite juffers oer 't lân, in moai ein fan har ôf. Sy gong der hinne om to sjen, mar doe wienen se samar fuort as snie foar de sinne. 't Gebeurde by de grouwe beam.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LINSSEN009501","role":"clip2","render":{"description":"Encounter with a lady without a head; digging up three chests of treasure fails because the silence is broken.","place":"Diergaarde","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208983","original":"Juffrouw zonder kop.. De paardeknecht van de boerderij \"de Horst\"onder de gemeente Echt, kwam 's avonds eens van de kermis thuis. Hij was over de grens geweest op Gulichs gebied en keerde door de bossen van \"de Doort\" terug. Hij had rijkelijk veel gedronken, raakte de weg kwijt en besloot maar te gaan liggen en de volgende morgen af te wachten. Juist hoorde hij de torenklok van Echt twaalf uur slaan en daarop aansluitend sloeg de klok van Dieteren (Susteren) ook twaalf. Dus Driekus, de knecht telde 24 slage n \"Zo laat ben ik nog nooit thuisgekomen\", dacht hij, \"wat is het hier toch een gekke boel, zowel met de weg als met de tijd.\"\nNauwelijks was hij ingeslapen of hij werd wakker door een vreemd geluid. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"TINNEV065","role":"clip3","render":{"description":"A man goes to cut grass stalks with six others when the first man suddenly starts screaming. The group starts running. When they have stopped running, the first man tells them he saw a grijze juffer (grey lady).","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0310F","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22411","original":"52.\nIk ging op een kier met zes andere smele sni'je bi'j Tengbarge. Bi'j de olde poort gekomme begon de veurste man ienéns had te krijse. Wi'j ginge allemaol lope. T oe wi'j een endje weg ware vetelle de eerste man datte een grieze juffer gezien had.","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KOOIJMAN0043","role":"inside","render":{"description":"In a churchyard a white, Madonna-like figure (transparent, wearing a small hood) rose up out of the ground. Beautiful, but also frightening. She rose straight up. It lasted only a few seconds, then she had vanished again.","place":"Stolwijkersluis","prov":"Z.-H.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50587","original":"Ik kwam samen met mijn broer van de Schielandse Hoge Zeedijk (1). We gingen langs de achterkant van het kerkhof aan de Bosweg (2). Toen zagen we samen midden uit de grond (3) een witte gedaante opstijgen. 't Was heel mooi, maar ook wel ietwat angstig. Ze had een kapje op, ze was net van glas en wit tot over haar voeten. Ze was doorzichtig en Madonna-achtig. Ze steeg omhoog, recht naar boven. Het duurde maar een paar seconden, toen was ze weer verdwenen.\n\n(1) de dijk van Gouda naar Moordrecht \n(2) in buitenwijk van Gouda \n(3) van het kerkhof","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","note":"This one I keep apart."},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Each story counts.","The first number is 2.","2 — 3 — 6."],"lock":{"kind":"number3","salt":"eb346f9c3519d33e","accepted_hashes":["0d41b3c3ee9804d5f7c38014b05067566811051b10b4cdfbbb3e7916d3c18325"]},"on_success":{"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3147,"rank":0.9293,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KEUNING012603","role":"member","render":{"description":"Two white women are said to walk in the churchyard at night.","place":"Genum","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131651","original":"Der waerd ek sein, dat op it tsjerkhôf to Hegebeintum by nacht faek twa wite wiven omrounen.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ124006","role":"member","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot witte wieven (white women) dance at night.","place":"Mûnein","prov":"Fr.","year":1979,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32288","original":"Oan 'e dyk to Readtsjerk spûken wite wiven, nei't se seinen. Dy dounsen dêr nachts om.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE070d","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator is heading home with a few friends. On the way they meet a white girl moving quickly. She floats towards a cottage. They go to investigate. Later an old man hanged himself, and people say it was connected with this. The minister is very sceptical about the story.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":null,"initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12149","original":"Wite juffers\nWat ik hjir yn 'e Westerein sels sjoen ha. Dat is no lyn, ik tink sa'n fiif-, seis-, sânenfyftich jier. Myn kammeraat en ik gyngen de jûntiid om in oere of alve stadichoan nei hûs ta. Doe troffen wy in pear jongelju en dy hâlden ús oan. De man sei: 'Sjoch, wat is dêr? Dêr is in famke midden yn 'e sûkerei. By it hûs dêre is it allegearre út en tsjuster, mar hoe kin dan sa'n wyt famke der yn 't lân weze?' Doe seach ik it ek. Ik sei: 'Dan moatte wy dêr ris even sjen'. Mar dat famke avensrarde tige hurd en wy koenen sjen, dat it net gie, mar dat it sweefde. It hie de grutte sawat fan in gewoan famke, en sniewyt. Ik sei: 'No, sille wy ris sjen? …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LIJST033","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"The devil follows a woman on her way home in the evening.","place":"Baflo","prov":"Gr.","year":1954,"code":null,"initials":"T.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/14752","original":"I. De duivel\n1. Zijn U verhalen bekend over mensen, die de duivel gezien hebben of omgang met hem hebben gehad (met hem gedanst hebben, met hem kaart hebben gespeeld), of kent U andere verhalen, waarin de duivel een rol speelt?\nGelieve elk verhaal te noteren op een afzonderlijk blad papier en in elk verhaal duidelijk aan te duiden hoe de duivel voorgesteld wordt (met bokshorens, bokspoten, paardenhoeven, sik, staat enz.).\n\nDit hoorde ik als kind; 1899 was het. De dochter van de vrouw die het overkwam vertelde het. Haar moeder was (ook al op leeftijd wel eens laat van de boerderij gekomen waar ze werkte, bij slacht en dergelijke kon het wel eens wat laat in de avond worden. Bij zoo'n gelegenheid was zij eens door de duivel gevolgd. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Baflo belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.1665,"rank":0.9831,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ045708","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man is startled at night by a white ghost woman who looks into all the cups on the table.","place":"Peize","prov":"Dr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24321","original":"Ik hie in omke Knjillis, dêr bin ik nei neamd. Hy plichte in soad by ús to kommen. Hy hie syn frou forlern en m_n frou wosk faek foar him.\nOp in kear kom er by ús, doe sei 'k: \"Knjillis-om, 'k leau, jo binne warch.\"\n\"Ja,\" sei er, \"ik bin èk warch.\"\n\"Omke docht doch neat mear, wol?\"\n\"Ik haw 't noch noait sa drok hawn as fannacht\", sei er.\n\"Hoedat sa?\" sei 'k.\n\"Ik lei op bêd justernacht en ik sjoch oer de keamer en doe wie dêr in wiif alhiel yn 't wyt. Dy giet om 'e tafel hinne en sjocht yn alle kopkes. Dy sjocht se allegear nei. Ja, en doe is se der út rekke.\nFannacht wie se der wer. Doe ha 'k mei har slein om se kwyt to wurden. Doe is se wer fuort rekke.\"\nOmke switte der oer en hie 't binaud.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KOOIJMAN0137","role":"card","render":{"description":"Near the Linschoten wood the haunting was so bad that the maids working for the farmers did not dare to go past it. There were ghosts in white.","place":"Haastrecht","prov":"Z.-H.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/50675","original":"Bij het Linschootse bos spookte het! Zo erg, dat de meiden die in de Linschoten bij de boeren werkten, d'r niet voorbij dorsten te gaan. Allegaar spoken in het wit!","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KEMP314","role":"card","render":{"description":"At the witching hour one night, Drikus meets a lady carrying her head in her hands. It happens at the spot where a castle once stood. The lady's head tells him he is lucky to have come on a Tuesday. Things would have gone badly for him on any other day.\nThe lady offers him the chance to dig up her money chests, which he may divide between himself, the poor and the church. The next Tuesday Drikus goes with his brother-in-law Hannes to dig up the treasure. But when Hannes says, 'Look, there sits the witch', the chests sink deeper than ever.","place":"Broek","prov":"L.","year":1925,"code":"SINSAG 0301","initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43441","original":"De juffrouw zonder kop\n\nDrikus was op een Vastenavonddinsdag naar het naburige Susteren geweest en had zich daar, bij zijn tante Seph, aan pannekoek en oud bier te goed gedaan, zodat het wel elf uur in de avond was, eer hij met een beneveld hoofd en wankelende schreden naar de Horst terugkeerde. Achter de Middelsgraaf, de grensscheiding tussen Echt en Susteren gekomen, sloeg hij, om de weg te korten, een voetpad in dat hem binnen een kwartier tijds door het Doert in de Horst zou brengen. Reeds had Drikus al meer dan een half uur rondgelopen en nog zag hij de hoeve in de heldere maneschijn niet voor zich opdagen. Hij doolde door hout- en struikgewas, verloor stilaan het begane pad en raakte in het meest woeste gedeelte van het bos. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ034801","role":"card","render":{"description":"Witte juffers (white maidens) haunt a haunted spot.","place":"Oudega","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22700","original":"Us mem biwearde, to Aldegea spoeke it op in smel reedtsje by Jan Japiksma. Dêr wie in boskje mei in gracht der omhinne. Dêr spoeken wite juffers.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"JCOHEN44","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Two neighbours' children grow up with stories about witte wieven (white women) and regularly see witte wieven themselves.\nThe master of ceremonies at their wedding forgets to invite the witte wief (white woman).\nDuring the wedding he goes to her after all, with a cat on a spit as a gift. He flings the spit at her and invites her to the wedding. The witte wief furiously chases him. He gets inside just in time and slams the door before the witte wief can get in. The spit she throws after him ends up in the wall and can still be seen.","place":"Zutphen","prov":"Gld.","year":1919,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"L.d.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/42094","stain":"two"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"ENGELB_08A_001","role":"card","render":{"description":"Dwelling place of witte wieven (white women); they are helpful, and if left alone they do nothing.","place":"Mander","prov":"Ov.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128452","original":"Bels: Doar hebt ze ok wat vuindn, nich, doe ze doar vrower an 't bouwn warn west, nich, en an 't eand har der dan nen kôm koffie of melk, dee har der kloar stoan zoa vertöln ze van oolds oet, nich.\nIk: Woar hebt dee witte wiew dan eigenlik in lewd dan?\nB: Dee hebt in de holn lewd.\nIk: Was dat een of andre beult, woar at ze inzatn?\nB: Joa ze zatn in ne beult, dat warn twee beultn, dee hebt ze later nog ôpgrövn, dokter Hijszeler is der wa met an 't grewn west met dee beultn, nich? …","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with Z.","Zutphen. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c5","object":"window","text":"Zutphen"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":2,"card":"c5","word":"two","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.679,"rank":0.375,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST274","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a wolf at night disappears when the farmer finds a wolfskin under his bed and burns it.","place":"Drogteropslagen","prov":"Dr.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"K.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13538","original":"Vroeger was hier een knecht, die 's nachts in een wolf veranderde en het de mensen dan lastig maakte. Onder zijn bed vond de boer op zekere dag een wolfshuid en verbrandde die. Sedert was de knecht verdwenen.\n(Verteld door een zeventig-jarige).","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VVUNL301","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand becomes a werewolf by means of a leather belt, which he hides. It is found and burnt in the oven; at once the suspected farmhand comes rushing up on horseback, but he is held back, and when the belt has burnt he says: \"I am freed!\"","place":"Echt","prov":"L.","year":1920,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"F.S.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35840","original":"De weerwolf \n\nOp de hoeve Bosscherhof woonde eertijds een knecht die een lederen riem bezat, welke de macht had, hem, indien hij hem omgordde, te betoveren als weerwolf. Geheimzinnig en zorgvuldig werd deze band telkenmale door de knecht verstopt en wat men ook deed, hoe men ook spiedde, men vond hem nooit. En geregeld hadden de mensen uit de omtrek, die laat huiswaarts keerden, de weerwolf te dragen. En ook iedereen herkende steeds de knecht. Men gaf elkander raad om wanneer men overvallen werd, de weerwolf op een of andere manier te prikken of te krab-ben tot hij bloed voelde of zag. Dan was men gered. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN002605","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a black cat at midnight by means of a rim is released after the rim is burned.","place":"Baexem","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208342","original":"Volgens tweede verteller was er op Nelishof te Tungelroy een knecht die elke nacht tussen twaalf en een uur afwezig was. Door een raampje ging hij naar buiten. Hij klom dan op de schansenhoop en kwam er als kat af. De boer had hem bespied en gemerkt dat boven op de schansenhoop een velg lag van een karwiel. Die had de boer daar niet neergelegd en hij zocht verband tussen de spokerij (zwarte kat) en dat karwiel.\nDit zou hij vernietigen als de knecht afwezig was. Op zekere dag had hij hem met schapen naar Antwerpen gestuurd. Toen hij een dag weg was stak de boer zijn bakoven aan en wierp de velg erin.\nOp hetzelfde moment verscheen de knecht en wilde de oven in. Het gelukte slechts met drie man om hem daarvan te weerhouden. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Limburg an animal was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1920.","That card names an animal. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"eb346f9c3519d33e","accepted_hashes":["2b7f85088c8299326df8943381301bcde188bb7807b29e01bf9e7834b29eb86e","4842ba42afac58431a01ca26ed951ebb36b6cac43a213940c24e73c7942b6b94","6096da431e002b4456194b90e59d3384056e66385771e1104e36f5fad4e4dc38","891ea267e180a11b9a46b7ae13c6c2564d52050764c082ea75a4336858bfdee7","d31c69b8718174a9390d851245fbedd734550d0d44899032ce255eec66c510fc"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.0563,"rank":0.462,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LINSSEN007605","role":"member","render":{"description":"Boy can change into a werewolf; after blood is drawn from the wolfhound, the boy's form appears.","place":"Leveroy","prov":"L.","year":1964,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208819","original":"Weerwolf. Een jongen bezat de macht om zich in een weerwolf te kunnen veranderen. Hij had verkering. Op zekere dag was hij met zijn aanstaande naar de kermis gegaan. In het struikgewas langs de weg gaf hij voor zijn behoefte te moeten doen. Tegen zijn verloofde zei hij, dat ze niet moest schrikken als er plotseling een wolf of een hond voorbij kwam. Het meisje werd bang, liep door en begaf zich naar een café, waar ze geheel onthutst aankwam. Nauwelijks was ze binnen of een wolfshond ging liggen onder de tafel, waaraan zij zat. Een van de aanwezigen had kwade vermoedens over het dier. Wanneer het een weerwolf was, zou hij nadat hem \"bloed\" getrokken was, weer een menselijke gedaante aannemen. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"ENGELS003711","role":"member","render":{"description":"After a fight with a werewolf it turns out to be someone known.","place":"Blerick","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"G.G.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/210804","original":"Weerwolven:\nEen man, die ’s avonds laat door een weerwolf werd besprongen, was hem te gauw af, door zich bliksemsnel om te draaien. Hij kreeg hem er onder. Het bleek een goede bekende van hem te zijn.\n\nGeen omzetting in dialect van het verhaal door Engels.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"GENDT088","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"One evening a woman meets a miller's hand who has a werewolf walking behind him. The man does not see it and the wolf disappears. That spot is haunted.","place":"Gendt","prov":"Gld.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"M.H.D.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/49723","original":"Ik kwam soaves es ’n keer Jans, de möldersknecht van Hoogveld, tège. Achter ’m liep ’n lillek dier. ’t Leek ’n werwolf. Hé’j had grote klauwe en gloeiende oge. Ik zèj: “Wa hè gé’j dor toch bé’j ou, Jans?” Hé’j zej:“Ik heb niks bé’j mien”. En toe was er ok niks mer. Da gebeurde op ten hoek bé’j de meule. De minse zèje, dat ’t dor altied spokte.","lang":"Gendt dialect (Achterhoek)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LINSSEN008310","role":"member","render":{"description":"After the werewolf that tries to jump on someone's back is wounded, it disappears.","place":"Posterholt","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208887","original":"Weerwolf Een jongeman uit de buurtschap Holst had kennis met een meisje uit de buurtschap Paalder (st. Odilienberg). Meermalen had hij over een grote afstand de weerwolf moeten dragen. Hij had bij anderen raad gevraagd, wat hij daartegen kon doen. Men had hem aangeraden een snijmes (groot breed mes, ongeveer 6o cm lang en 1o cm breed , om stro te snijden met aan beide kanten een houten handvat.) op de rug te binden met de scherpe kant naar achteren gericht. Zo gezegd, zo gedaan. De eerstvolgende keer dat de weerwolf hem weer besprong liet deze een rauwe kreet horen, vluchtte weg en nooit meer had de man last van hem gehad.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Gendt belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0554,"rank":0.4872,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"EDJSL012","role":"card","render":{"description":"A day labourer is returning home and sees a plough with no horse or man coming towards him. The plough changes shape: it is the smallholder, standing before him. The smallholder begs the man not to give him away.\nAt haymaking time the two men work together. When the smallholder is asleep, a mole comes out of his neck. The smallholder vomits litres of blood. In the meadow the remains of a calf are found; only a few gnawed bones are left. The smallholder dies. The priest has to come before the coffin can be carried to the churchyard.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1980,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"E.d.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9514","original":"Mol, de weerwolf\nEen keuterboer, die Mol heette, werd altijd uitgescholden:\n\"Bierpoep! Twee emmers vol snijbonen en nog maar wind!\"\nDat kwam omdat hij zoveel at.\nKarels, een dagloner, keerde 's avonds laat dwars door het veld terug naar huis, toen hij een ploeg zonder paard of man op zich af zag komen. Hij trok zijn mes, maar het ketste af op het ploegijzer. De ploeg veranderde van gedaante, en in de man die voor hem stond, herkende hij Mol.\nDeze viel op zijn knieën en smeekte hem niet te verraden. Hij zou Karels een mud boekweit en een mud rogge geven.\n\"Van jou, weerwolf, wil ik geen boekweit of rogge,\" zei de boerenknecht. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"VODA_002_09","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of seven sons is a werewolf. Werewolves can also be recognised by their eyebrows that meet in the middle.","place":"Eindhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1976,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/69626","original":"Als een vader zeven zonen had dan was een van die zeven zonen een weerwolf. ‘T is wel zo dat, bij een elkele vorige uitzending het had over de heksen, om een heks zo te kunnen herkennen, en zo herkent men ook de weerwolven. En in hoofdzaak kent men dan de weerwolven, want die moesten weer een teken van de duivel hebben, natuurlijk, dat [eh], samengegroeide wenkbrauwen hadden he. Mensen die samengegroeide wenkbrauwen hadden die waren voorbestemd om [om, om, om, om] weerwolf te zijn, he. En verder ter war, verder kon men dan, men kon dus eerst in [eh] weerwolf worden door een verbond te sluiten met de duivel en dan kregen ze doorlopende wenkbrauwen want dan kon de duivel ze herkennen.","lang":"Brabant dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"door","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","3 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c5","object":"door","n":3},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.5916,"rank":0.7124,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ080801","role":"target","render":{"description":"A maidservant always heard someone haunting at the churning mill at one o'clock at night. But when she went to look, there was never anyone to be seen. The previous farmer had hanged himself at that churning mill and always haunted it afterwards.","place":null,"prov":"Fr.","year":1970,"code":"SINSAG 0435","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/29363","original":"Us mem hat by in boer tsjinne. Doe wie se noch jong.\nNachts om ien ûre hearde ús mem altyd ien de mjilling lâns sliere. De oaren hearden it soms ek. Mar noait ien dy't hwat seach. Se bigongen der allegearre om to tinken en se hearden sekuer it sloffen troch de koestâl, it gong nei de tsjernmoune ta. Mar as se der ôf gongen om to sjen hwat it wie, seagen se noait hwat.\nDe eardere boer hie him dêr oan 'e tsjernmoune ophong.\nDy mat dêr letter altyd omspûke ha. Mem hat it ús faek forteld.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ007509","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A barn is haunted. In a certain spot in the barn no one can sleep. Whoever does is lifted up and thrown a long way off. Someone is said to have hanged himself there once.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0435","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/16998","original":"Yn Uthuzen (Uithuizen, Gr.) stiet in skuorre, dat is in spûkskuorre. De boer dy't op dy pleats wenne, hiet fan Biesterveld. Dêr wie in plak yn 'e skuorre, dêr koe it wurkfolk net sliepe. Dy't dat weage, waerd optild en in ein fuortsmiten. Der waerd altyd foar warskôge, dat men dêr net sliepe moest. Men woe wol ha, dat him dêr ris ien forhong hat.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1","geo":[53.26224,6.07544]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ047601","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A farmhand spending the night in a haunted barn sees a little light moving over the walls at night. It is said that someone once hanged himself in the barn.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0435","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24570","original":"Der wienen us guon út 'e Westerein nei in boer yn Den Andel ta to wjûden. Myn suster Minke wie der ek by. Sy moesten de nachts yn in boereskuorre sliepe en dy skuorre dat wie in spûkskuorre.\nMidden yn 'e nacht seach myn suster in ljochtsje by de muorre lâns gean en dêrnei nei de oare muorre ta.\nIn man fan 'e Westerein sei tsjin har: \"It spûket hjir, Minke, sjochst it wol?\"\n\"Jawol\", hie Minke sein.\nIt ljochtsje wie wer nei 't selde plak ta gien as dêr't it weikom wie.\nDe keppelbaes Megiel Folkerts woe net lije dat se der fierder oer praetten.\nIt sechje gong, dat de heit fan Megiel Folkerts him dêr froeger ophong hie.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1","geo":[53.25731,6.0363]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ049219","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A barn where a girl once hanged herself is haunted.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0435","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24685","original":"By de Houtigehaechster wyk (= Skoallewyk) wenne âlde Karst. Dêr hat in jongfaem har al ris ophong. Yn 'e skuorre. Sûnt dy tiid spûke it dêr. Wy doarsten dêr jouns net lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1","geo":[53.08284,6.04578]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Kollumersweach.","Find Harkema on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[53.18333,6.13333],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Harkema"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3232,"rank":0.948,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KEUNING013202","role":"member","render":{"description":"Haunting in a churchyard; the ghosts at a farm turn out to be a courting couple.","place":"Ferwert","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131689","original":"Op it tsjerkhôf spûke it. Dêr kaem jouns net ien lâns. En sa wie it oan 'e singel by in greate pleats ek. Der wienen forskeidene, dy dêr hwat sjoen hienen. Mar letter blykte it, dat it in pearke wie, dat dêr efter de beamkes forskûle oan it frijen wie.\nDe faem mocht fan thús net mei dy jonge.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ115001","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"When it is foggy in a certain place, people say the witte wieven (white women) are holding a meeting.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1977,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/30997","original":"To Feanwâldsterwâl seinen se mei mistich waer as der fan dy mistslierten wienen en it rûze hwat yn 'e reiden: \"Hearst it wol? De wite wiven binne oan 't forgaderjen.\"","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"BIJLSMA000511","role":"member","render":{"description":"At a farm where a monastery once stood, people see and hear things.","place":"Raerd","prov":"Fr.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"T.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/130196","original":"Dêr op Hazzebuorren stiet ek in pleats, dy't men it kleaster neamt. Foar in fyftich jier wenne Sybren Swierstra dêr. Dêr hat alear in kleaster stien. Dêr seach en hearde men ek hwat.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ030302","role":"member","render":{"description":"If the gable sign of a certain farm, a skull, is removed, the haunting begins.","place":"Oosterwierum","prov":"Fr.","year":1951,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21936","original":"Under Achlum stie in pleats, dêr stie in deadskop op. As se dy der wei dienen, dan wienen se forlegen yn 'e hûs, sa gong 't der dan oan wei. Dy deadskop moest der op.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Burgum belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1885,"rank":0.7083,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CBAK0376","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer on a haunted farm asks a begging old soldier whether he will keep watch at night.","place":"Uitdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1903,"code":"SINSAG 0401","initials":"C.B.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/9190","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ081008","role":"half","render":{"description":"There at the roadside they saw a giant, fully twice the size of a normal person. A large cloak flapped around him; otherwise he stood completely still. It was a ghost.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"BIJLSMA003301","role":"half","render":{"description":"After his death his widow hears in the evenings the same sound her husband made when he went upstairs. Visitors go to look and hear knocking at a book. When it is picked up, the papers fall out of the book.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ058107","role":"half","render":{"description":"Suddenly they saw a fellow wearing a hat. When he passed them, he suddenly vanished.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0475"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CBAK0513","role":"half","render":{"description":"The answer is that they have waited a long time for someone, that there is money buried of which he may have a third, and the rest must go in equal parts to the poor and a church congregation. Once the request has been carried out, the haunting stops.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ015103","role":"half","render":{"description":"As the man and his new bride are about to get into the carriage, his dead wife suddenly appears. She reminds him of his promise and the newlyweds undo the marriage. The spirit of the dead can only find rest once a promise made before death is kept.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CBAK0376","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"At midnight, after a lot of noise, six high-ranking officers with sabres come in and go to the haystack. There they dig a hole, take out a kettle of gold coins, bury it again and leave. With a farmhand's help the beggar digs up the kettle. The next night they keep watch together and see the men come again, who leave and never come back when they find nothing. The soldier stays on the farm. According to the narrator it was providence that the soldier was meant to have the money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401","stain":"six"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘farm’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0401. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c7","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c7"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":6,"card":"c1","word":"six","stained":"c7"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
